## State machine

Pickup gating is enforced by the existing runner pre-pickup gate
(`backend.agents.file_coordinator.has_unresolved_blockedby`). Every
child sits in `To Do` until its declared blocker reaches Published.
The chain is strictly sequential by default (R1 → R2 → ... → R13);
template authors may declare additional `blocked_by` entries to
serialise across non-adjacent children.

## Recovery

If instantiation fails partway through the script:

1. The script writes the created ticket keys to
   `/tmp/release-rollback-{version}.json` before exiting non-zero.
2. The operator runs `scripts/instantiate_release_meta.py
   --rollback {version}` (G2 — not yet shipped) or deletes the
   listed tickets by hand.
3. Re-running the script without `--force` refuses while the META
   key exists; deleting the META and the rollback file is the
   supported way to reset.

`--force` is reserved for the rare case where the META was Archived
(workflow-cleaned) but the operator needs a fresh instance — it
bypasses the `MetaAlreadyExists` guard. Use `--dry-run` first.

## Acceptance criteria (META)

- [ ] All 13 children (`R1`..`R13`) created with correct labels and AC
- [ ] `blockedBy` chain wired in the L-OP-874 direction (inward=blocker,
      outward=blocked)
- [ ] Each child carries a `Relates` link back to this META
- [ ] Operator-readable child map comment landed within 30 seconds of
      META creation
- [ ] Closing R13 transitions this META to Published (see R13 AC)

